Derive the following Entropy of Reversible and Free Expansion relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
\Delta S_{\mathrm{gas}}
=\frac{Q_{\mathrm{rev}}}{T}
=nR\ln\!\left(\frac{V_f}{V_i}\right).
\tag*{[3]}
\]
Notation: \(n\) denotes amount of ideal gas; unit \(\mathrm{mol}\); \(R\) denotes molar gas constant; unit \(\mathrm{J mol^{-1} K^{-1}}\); \(T\) denotes constant absolute gas temperature; unit \(\mathrm{K}\); \(p,V\) denotes equilibrium gas pressure and total volume; unit \(\mathrm{Pa, m^{3}}\); \(V_i,V_f\) denotes initial and final gas volumes; unit \(\mathrm{m^{3}, m^{3}}\); \(Q,W\) denotes heat transferred into the gas and work done by the gas; unit \(\mathrm{J, J}\); \(Q_{\mathrm{rev}},W_{\mathrm{rev}}\) denotes heat transferred into the gas and work done by the gas along the reversible comparison path; unit \(\mathrm{J, J}\); \(\Delta U\) denotes change in gas internal energy; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{gas}},\Delta S_{\mathrm{surr}},\Delta S_{\mathrm{univ}}\) denotes entropy changes of gas, surroundings, and gas plus surroundings; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}, J K^{-1}, J K^{-1}}\); \(S_{\mathrm{gen}}\) denotes entropy generated in the chosen composite; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\).

